  "worked_solution": "Here, we are dividing a negative number $(-25)$ by a positive one $(5).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n(-25)÷5=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $25$ by $5$ without any signs: $25÷5=5.$ Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n(-25)÷5=-5.\n$$",
